  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2314216386f93e848b802d3e5aa8e609, type: 3}
  m_Name: Mechanical Low Back Pain
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MedicalCase
  title: Mechanical Low Back Pain
  type: Common
  category: Musculoskeletal
  description: Pain, stiffness, and/or soreness of the lumbosacral region, located
    underneath the twelfth rib and above the gluteal folds. It is the most common
    cause of decreased productivity among the working population in the Philippines.
  symptoms: 'Lower back pain that is often on and off.   Difficulty lifting heavy
    objects.   Absence of red flags such as fever, neurologic deficits, or bowel/bladder
    incontinence. '
  pathology: Generally non-specific and mechanical in nature, often caused by heavy
    lifting or occupational strain.
  treatment: 'First-line pharmacotherapy includes oral non-steroidal anti-inflammatory
    drugs (NSAIDs).   Non-pharmacological approaches like patient education, return
    to normal activity, and self-care temperature treatments (ice, heat) are preferred.  '
  keyFeatures: Evaluation should use the Look-Move-Feel Approach and screen for red
    flags using the BACK PAINS mnemonic to rule out secondary underlying pathology.
  requiredStageLevel: 1
